xfce4-bsdbluetooth-plugin manages Bluetooth on FreeBSD, as blueman-applet
does on Linux, with the base system's Bluetooth stack and daemons:

- an XFCE panel plugin: Bluetooth on and off, the devices set up before
  (connect state, disconnect, remove), search for devices in range and
  pair them; keyboards get a PIN to type, mice and keyboards are handed to
  bthidd(8);
- bsdbt, the same from the command line;
- bsdbt-helper, a small root helper run through pkexec with a polkit
  policy that allows the user at the console.  It edits the configuration
  of hcsecd(8) and bthidd(8) one device at a time and pairs through HCI.

Bluetooth Classic devices only (the FreeBSD stack has no Bluetooth Low
Energy input devices).
